WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Yes, I remember that deposition very . . . I remember the one that I went to very well.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.340
I went with my father, and I think it was Bob Carter.

3
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.700
The thing that I remembered most about it,

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:24.140
because I didn’t quite know what to expect—I’d never been to a deposition before—was the presentation that Leander Perez made.

5
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:24.760
My mother went.

6
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.820
My mother went, I remember that now.

7
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:38.220
Leander Perez, in either summarizing some information or whatever . . . He was very colorful.

8
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:46.560
He was dressed in a sort of a plantation beige outfit with a sort of a string tie, or whatever.

9
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.300
He was a very colorful character and used a lot of flamboyant language.

10
00:00:52.300 --> 00:01:00.240
Was very dramatic and also could be very cruel and biting and sarcastic.

11
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.980
He was known around New Orleans and around Louisiana for his hatred,

12
00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:16.160
hatred of black people and mistreatment of the people that worked for him or worked for his family and all that kind of stuff.

13
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.640
One statement that he made that I’ll never forget, because this was a long time ago,

14
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:29.380
was . . . He pointed to me and walked in my direction and looked right dead at me and said that,

15
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:36.180
“There sits the only ungrateful nigra in the state of Louisiana.

16
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:45.980
Because we have gone to great expense and trouble to build up fine black universities in this state.

17
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:55.560
Why is Mr. Tureaud not willing to avail himself of this opportunity?”

18
00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:02.740
He said it with such sarcasm and with such belief.

19
00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.300
It was just very intimidating and I . . . It made me angry.
